# Error Handling Patterns

## Async Handler Wrapper

```typescript
const asyncHandler = (fn: RequestHandler): RequestHandler => {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    Promise.resolve(fn(req, res, next)).catch(next);
  };
};
```

## Global Error Middleware

```typescript
const errorHandler: ErrorRequestHandler = (err, req, res, _next) => {
  if (err instanceof AppError) {
    return res.status(err.statusCode).json({
      error: err.code,
      message: err.message,
    });
  }

  // Unexpected error — log and return generic message
  console.error('Unexpected error:', err);
  return res.status(500).json({
    error: 'INTERNAL_ERROR',
    message: 'An unexpected error occurred',
  });
};
```

## Service Error Pattern

```typescript
async function getTaskById(id: string): Promise<Task> {
  const task = await prisma.task.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  if (!task) throw new NotFoundError('Task', id);
  return task;
}
```

## Never Do

- `catch (e) { /* swallow */ }` — never silently swallow errors
- `res.status(500).json({ error: err.message })` — never expose raw error messages
- `throw new Error("not found")` — always use typed AppError subclasses
